{"nodes": [{"id": "docs_adr_0024_a_parent_and_its_subtasks_are_one_piece_of_work", "label": "ADR 0024 A parent and its subtasks are one piece of work", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/adr/0024-a-parent-and-its-subtasks-are-one-piece-of-work.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "docs_adr_0024_a_parent_and_its_subtasks_are_one_piece_of_work_count_subtasks", "label": "orgConfig.countSubtasks (default false)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0024-a-parent-and-its-subtasks-are-one-piece-of-work.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Subtasks inflate item counts by decomposition habit exactly as points inflate by estimation; whether subtasks even arrive varies by board type and route, so the product could not say what its counts included. Uses Jira's issuetype.subtask flag, never the type name; absent means not a subtask."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0024_a_parent_and_its_subtasks_are_one_piece_of_work_counted_types", "label": "orgConfig.countedTypes allow-list (default empty)", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/adr/0024-a-parent-and-its-subtasks-are-one-piece-of-work.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Empty means every type the subtask rule left; naming types per site means a new type silently stops counting."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0024_a_parent_and_its_subtasks_are_one_piece_of_work_counting_reported_beside_figures", "label": "facts.meta.counting / forecast.inputs.counting", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0024-a-parent-and-its-subtasks-are-one-piece-of-work.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Reports seen, counted and not counted whether or not anything was excluded; a key present only sometimes reads as nothing when absent."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0024_a_parent_and_its_subtasks_are_one_piece_of_work_reader_type_filter", "label": "Reader's issue-type filter", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0024-a-parent-and-its-subtasks-are-one-piece-of-work.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Lists types the board actually uses; narrows the organisation's rule and never widens it (expressed as an effective config so counted_issues stays the one implementation); travels with the forecast request and cache key; selecting nothing is a refusal per ADR 0010."}, {"id": "docs_adr_0024_a_parent_and_its_subtasks_are_one_piece_of_work_parent_and_subtasks_are_one_item", "label": "A parent and its subtasks are one item", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/adr/0024-a-parent-and-its-subtasks-are-one-piece-of-work.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Filtering in the producer was rejected because it discards the raw issues and a config change would need a refetch; the rule is applied where figures are made, in Python and mirrored in JavaScript."}], "edges": [{"source": "docs_adr_0024_a_parent_and_its_subtasks_are_one_piece_of_work", "target": "docs_adr_0024_a_parent_and_its_subtasks_are_one_piece_of_work_count_subtasks", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0024-a-parent-and-its-subtasks-are-one-piece-of-work.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "docs_adr_0024_a_parent_and_its_subtasks_are_one_piece_of_work", "target": "docs_adr_0024_a_parent_and_its_subtasks_are_one_piece_of_work_counted_types", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/adr/0024-a-parent-and-its-subtasks-are-one-piece-of-work.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source"